<BaseLayout
  title="Architecture"
  description="How the workstation, project repos, CI, and cluster fit together."
  currentPath="/architecture"
>
  <section class="content-body">
    <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
    <h1>How It Fits Together</h1>
    <p>
      Most of what I build goes through the same small pipeline. Here's the shape of it,
      from my laptop to a live URL.
    </p>

    <pre><code>┌─────────────────┐
│    dev-setup     │  workstation — Nix flakes, Home Manager, Homebrew
└────────┬─────────┘
         │ write, build, commit
         v
┌─────────────────┐
│  project repos   │  byah, deckforge, landlordlog, collections,
│                  │  reliquary-works, cutty-bangerz, slopyard,
│                  │  choose-your-own-game-theory, and others
└────────┬─────────┘
         │ CI — test, build image, push
         v
┌─────────────────┐
│     homelab      │  k3s GitOps source of truth
└────────┬─────────┘
         │ reconciles on commit
         v
┌─────────────────┐
│   k3s cluster    │  Hetzner VPS — ingress, secrets, backing services
└────────┬─────────┘
         │ serves
         v
   live sites (byah.org, deckforge.byah.org, drank.byah.org, ...)</code></pre>

    <p>
      <a href="/projects/dev-setup/">dev-setup</a> is the machine I write everything on — a
      Nix-managed macOS environment, not something that ever gets deployed. Each project
      lives in its own repo with its own stack, but they share the same path out: CI tests
      the code, builds a container image, and pushes it. <a href="/projects/homelab/">homelab</a>
      is where that image becomes a running thing — it holds the k3s manifests and pins the
      image tags, and the cluster reconciles to match on commit. From there, ingress and DNS
      turn it into a URL you can actually visit.
    </p>
    <p>
      Not everything runs through this loop. <a href="/projects/agents/">agents</a>,
      <a href="/projects/code-practice/">code-practice</a>, and
      <a href="/projects/project-planner/">project-planner</a> are local tools I never
      deploy — they're meant to be run, not visited.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
